 "_comment": [
  "English for text that the program code references directly. Built by tools/ui.py.",
  "strings: id = ROM address of the original. 'en' is a list of lines (same count as 'zh'), or null",
  "  to keep the original. A line may be a list of segments [zh, en, (max px)]: each English",
  "  segment is drawn where its Chinese segment started (menus copy fixed rectangles of the",
  "  text canvas, so each segment must fit its slot; the build checks it).",
  "  A 4th segment value forces its x (pixels from the line start).",
  "  'adv' = [2-byte, 1-byte] advance used by that screen, to place segments.",
  "  'max_px' = width limit for plain lines.",
  "layout: byte overrides for the menu layout scripts (see tools/layout.py).",
  "names: party names (menus/battle), 48 px each. descriptions: item help line, 144 px."
